    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1147" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδάμ-ᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδάμαστος</span>
			, <i>unconquered</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Th.</u>
				233
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				205
			</span></i>, etc.: of females, <i>unwedded</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				450
			</span></i>; <i>untamed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόσχος ἀ. πέσημα δίκε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					640
				</span></i>
			.—Trag. word, always in lyr. (exc. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
			</span></i>l.c); restored by Elmsl. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδάμαντος</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-αστος</span>
